    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Append a File Using ofstream"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "To append a file, we first need to create an ofstream object, then pass ios::app as an argument to the open() function."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "// create object of ofstream\nofstream my_file;\n\n// open file in append mode\nmy_file.open(\"cpp.txt\", ios::app);"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Now, let's append the string \"\\nThis is an appended content.\" to the cpp.txt file. Here, '\\n' means, we are appending the content in a new line."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "#include <fstream>\n#include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n\n\n    // open file in append mode\n    ofstream my_file;\n    my_file.open(\"cpp.txt\", ios::app);\n\n\n    // check if file is open or has any errors\n    if (my_file.fail()) {\n        cout << \"Error! Cannot open cpp.txt!\";\n        exit(0);\n    }\n\n    // add content to the file\n    my_file << \"\\nThis is an appended content.\";\n\n    my_file.close();\n\n    return 0;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, we have opened the file in append mode. So, the following code adds the string \"\\nThis is an appended content.\" to cpp.txt without erasing its previous content."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "my_file << \"\\nThis is an appended content\";"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "When we run the program, the new content of the cpp.txt file will be"
    },
